{
	title: 'Terminal tool results continue their call card',
	spec: 'In the terminal, a tool result drawn right under its call (or under another result of the same call) continues the call card: no blank row between them, the call card loses its bottom padding row, and the result has its own top and bottom padding rows. The result background is the call card hue 0.03 darker in lightness; its text has the call hue at a third of its chroma, 0.03 darker, unquieted; an error uses the error colour. Result rows and live tool output start at the text margin: no marker and no two-column indent. A failed result first row starts with ✗ so an error is not told by colour alone. A result apart from its call keeps the #<call> link prefix and the quiet log colour without a background. The web is unchanged (ask the user before mirroring).',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'frame.layout pops the call card bottom padding row before an attached result. ends[] for the call still counts that row, so a resumed layout that slices to it pops again: the cache stays consistent. The call tool name is found by walking back over results of the same id, since results carry only the id.'
	],
	needs: ['ap'],
	foldInto: ['ap', 'cc']
}
